,title,link,text,language,family
0,Ayautla Mazatec - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayautla_Mazatec,"Ayautla Mazatec is a Mazatecan language spoken in the Mexican state of Oaxaca, in the town of San Bartolomé Ayautla. Egland (1978) found 80% intelligibility with Huautla, the prestige variety of Mazatec.","Mazatec, Ayautla",Otomanguean
1,Oto-Manguean languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oto-Manguean_languages,"In 1865, Pimentel added Mazatec, Popoloca, Chatino, and Chinantec and also posed a separate group of Pame, Otomi and Mazahua, the beginning of the Oto-Pamean sub-branch.","Mazatec, Ayautla",Otomanguean
