3,"Mazatec, Ayautla language resources | Joshua ProjectMazatec, Ayautla Language (VMY) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status ...Mazatec Language and the Mazateco Indian Tribe (Mazateca)Keeping the Mazatec Language Alive Through Song",https://joshuaproject.net/languages/vmy,"Listing of people groups speaking Mazatec, Ayautla. Mazatec, Ayautla dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability. Ayautla Mazatec is a stable indigenous language of Mexico. It belongs to the Otomanguean language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools. Mazatec is an Oto-Manguean language of Mexico. There are eight different varieties of Mazatec, which are considered separate languages by some people and dialects of the same language by others. Oct 13, 2025 · We sat together around a table in their home, listening as they shared both their concerns about the loss of Mazatec culture and traditions, and their ideas and prayers for how to keep them alive.","Mazatec, Ayautla",Otomanguean
